	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type "eject" in Alfred to safely eject every external physical disk (USB / Thunderbolt, including drives on a dock).

The work is done by ~/bin/eject-all (installed by https://github.com/nixsiow/mac-tools), which:
  - never touches the internal SSD, the boot disk, disk images or network shares
  - stops a running Time Machine backup and waits for it to finish cleanly first
  - never force-ejects
  - posts a notification: "Safe to unplug" or "Do NOT unplug yet" with the reason

Run "eject-all --help" in a terminal for CLI options (dry-run, timeout, verbose).
Log: ~/Library/Logs/eject-all.log</string>
